# DemoSpring - API route tests
# Dataset: tp-spring-10-aventures.sql (100 departments, 1002 cities)
# Run in IntelliJ HTTP Client or `httpie`/`curl` equivalents.
#
# Conventions after the Tier-1 refactor:
#  - every FAILURE returns the same JSON: {timestamp, status, error, message, path}
#  - POST -> 201 + the created resource
#  - PUT  -> 200 + the updated resource
#  - DELETE -> 204, empty body
#  - search endpoints -> 200 + [] when nothing matched (never 400)
#  - constrained path/query ints (id, page, size, n, min, max) -> 400 when out of range

@host = http://localhost:8080

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### DEPARTMENTS
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### [1] List all departments -> 200
GET {{host}}/departments

### [2] Get department by id -> 200
GET {{host}}/departments/7

### [3] Get department by unknown id -> 404
GET {{host}}/departments/99999

### [4] Create department, duplicate code -> 400 "already exists"
POST {{host}}/departments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "34",
  "name": "Herault"
}

### [5] Create department, blank code -> 400 "code: Department code cannot be blank."
POST {{host}}/departments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "",
  "name": "X"
}

### [6] Create department, new code -> 201 + the created department
POST {{host}}/departments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "ZZ",
  "name": "Testland"
}

### [7] Update department -> 200 + the updated department
###     (set :id to the ZZ department created above)
PUT {{host}}/departments/102
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "ZZ",
  "name": "Renamed"
}

### [8] Update department, unknown id -> 404
PUT {{host}}/departments/99999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "QQ"
}

### [9] Delete department -> 204, empty body  (cleanup; set :id to the ZZ department)
DELETE {{host}}/departments/102

### [10] Delete department, unknown id -> 404
DELETE {{host}}/departments/99999

### [11] Get department, id 0 -> 400 (@Positive)
GET {{host}}/departments/0


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### CITIES - reads
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### [12] List cities, paginated -> 200
GET {{host}}/cities?page=1&size=2

### [13] Get city by id -> 200 (Paris)
GET {{host}}/cities/13321

### [14] Get city by unknown id -> 404
GET {{host}}/cities/999999

### [15] Get city by exact name (case-insensitive) -> 200
GET {{host}}/cities/search/name/Lyon 3e Arrondissement

### [16] Get city by unknown name -> 404
GET {{host}}/cities/search/name/Atlantis

### [17] Cities whose name starts with a prefix -> 200
GET {{host}}/cities/search/startswith/Saint-Bri

### [18] Prefix with no match -> 200 + []
GET {{host}}/cities/search/startswith/Zzz

### [19] Population strictly greater than -> 200 (desc)
GET {{host}}/cities/search/population/greater/800000

### [20] Population greater than, no match -> 200 + []
GET {{host}}/cities/search/population/greater/99999999

### [21] Population strictly between (bounds exclusive) -> 200
GET {{host}}/cities/search/population/between/400000/900000

### [22] Population between, no match -> 200 + []
GET {{host}}/cities/search/population/between/1/2

### [23] N largest cities of a department -> 200
GET {{host}}/cities/search/department/48/largest/5

### [24] Largest cities of unknown department -> 200 + []
GET {{host}}/cities/search/department/99999/largest/5

### [25] Cities of a department, population between -> 200
GET {{host}}/cities/search/department/48/population/between/40000/90000

### [26] Cities of a department, population greater than (alt route) -> 200
GET {{host}}/cities/department/48/population/greater-than/100000


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### CITIES - writes
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### [27] Create city, valid -> 201 + the created city
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Testville",
  "population": 1234,
  "departmentCode": "34"
}

### [28] Create city, name too short -> 400 "name: City name must contain at least 2 letters."
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A",
  "population": 10,
  "departmentCode": "34"
}

### [29] Create city, name + population both invalid -> 400, BOTH reported
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A",
  "population": 0
}

### [30] Create city, no department -> 400 "Unknown department."
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nodept",
  "population": 10
}

### [31] Create city, duplicate in department -> 400 "already exists"
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Testville",
  "population": 9999,
  "departmentCode": "34"
}

### [32] Update city -> 200 + the updated city  (set :id to the Testville city)
PUT {{host}}/cities/14324
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Testville2",
  "population": 5000,
  "departmentCode": "34"
}

### [33] Update city, unknown id -> 404
PUT {{host}}/cities/999999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ghost",
  "population": 5,
  "departmentCode": "34"
}

### [34] Delete city -> 204, empty body  (set :id to the Testville city)
DELETE {{host}}/cities/14324

### [35] Delete city, unknown id -> 404
DELETE {{host}}/cities/999999


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### EDGE CASES / WEIRD VALUES
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### [E1] Non-numeric path var -> 400 "Parameter 'id' must be of type int."
GET {{host}}/cities/abc

### [E2] Float path var -> 400
GET {{host}}/cities/1.5

### [E3] Value above int range -> 400
GET {{host}}/cities/99999999999999

### [E4] Negative id -> 400 (@Positive)
GET {{host}}/cities/-5

### [E5] id 0 -> 400 (@Positive)
GET {{host}}/cities/0

### [E6] page size 0 -> 400 (getCities.size: must be >= 1)
GET {{host}}/cities?page=0&size=0

### [E7] negative page -> 400 (@Min(0))
GET {{host}}/cities?page=-1&size=5

### [E8] negative size -> 400 (@Min(1))
GET {{host}}/cities?page=0&size=-3

### [E9] page far beyond data -> 200, empty content
GET {{host}}/cities?page=99999&size=5

### [E10] non-numeric page param -> 400
GET {{host}}/cities?page=x&size=5

### [E11] largest/0 -> 400 (@Positive on n)
GET {{host}}/cities/search/department/48/largest/0

### [E12] largest/-1 -> 400
GET {{host}}/cities/search/department/48/largest/-1

### [E13] population between with min > max (both >= 0) -> 200 + [] (no match)
GET {{host}}/cities/search/population/between/900000/1

### [E14] population greater than negative -> 400 (@PositiveOrZero)
GET {{host}}/cities/search/population/greater/-1

### [E15] PATCH on a city -> 405 Method Not Allowed
PATCH {{host}}/cities/13321

### [E16] Unknown route -> 404 "No endpoint GET /villes."
GET {{host}}/villes

### [E17] Trailing slash -> 404 (Spring no longer matches by default)
GET {{host}}/cities/13321/

### [E18] Empty request body -> 400 "Malformed or unreadable request body."
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

### [E19] Empty JSON object -> 400, both fields: "name: ... cannot be null.; population: ... at least 1 ..."
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### [E20] Malformed JSON -> 400 "Malformed or unreadable request body."
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":

### [E21] Wrong scalar type (population as text) -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Xy", "population": "lots", "departmentCode": "34" }

### [E22] Content-Type text/plain -> 415 Unsupported Media Type
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: text/plain

{ "name": "Zpp", "population": 5, "departmentId": 1 }

### [E23] name = "  " (two spaces) -> 201 CREATED  !! still weak (Tier-2 item 13):
###       @Size(min=2) passes on whitespace, no @NotBlank / trim. Clean up after.
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "  ", "population": 5, "departmentId": 1 }

### [E24] Unknown departmentId only -> 400 "Unknown department."
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zqww", "population": 5, "departmentId": 88888 }

### [E25] Unknown departmentCode -> 201 and SILENTLY CREATES department "QX1"
###       (documented behaviour of DepartmentService.resolve; Tier-2 item).
###       Clean up both city and dept.
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ghosttown", "population": 5, "departmentCode": "QX1" }

### [E26] Unknown JSON field is ignored -> 201 (city created). Clean up.
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zrr", "population": 5, "departmentId": 1, "bogus": 123 }

### [E27] Case-insensitive duplicate: "PARIS" in dept 37 -> 400 "already exists"
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "PARIS", "population": 1, "departmentId": 37 }

### [E28] Department code = "   " (spaces) -> 400 "code: Department code cannot be blank."
POST {{host}}/departments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "   ", "name": "x" }

### [E29] Exact-name lookup does NOT trim: "Paris " -> 404
GET {{host}}/cities/search/name/Paris%20

### [E30] startswith is case-insensitive: "paris" -> 200
GET {{host}}/cities/search/startswith/paris


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────
### TYPE MISMATCH — deliberately wrong values in numeric fields
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### --- text where an int is expected: PATH / QUERY (all clean 400) ---

### [T1] letters in a path int -> 400
GET {{host}}/departments/abc

### [T2] letters in a search int -> 400
GET {{host}}/cities/search/population/greater/abc

### [T3] letters in second path int -> 400
GET {{host}}/cities/search/population/between/10/abc

### [T4] letters in department id -> 400
GET {{host}}/cities/search/department/xx/largest/5

### [T5] letters in the N of largest/N -> 400
GET {{host}}/cities/search/department/48/largest/five

### [T6] Spring parses leniently: "+5" -> id 5 (valid, so -> 404 no such city)
GET {{host}}/cities/+5

### --- wrong JSON types in the request body ---

### [T7] population = "lots"  -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": "lots", "departmentId": 1 }

### [T8] population = 12.5  -> 201 !! Jackson ACCEPT_FLOAT_AS_INT truncates to 12
###      (Tier-2: disable ACCEPT_FLOAT_AS_INT). Clean up the created city.
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": 12.5, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T9] population = "10" (numeric string) -> 201 !! Jackson coerces to 10
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt10", "population": "10", "departmentId": 1 }

### [T10] population = true -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": true, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T11] population = null -> 400 (cannot map null into primitive int)
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": null, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T12] population = [] -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": [], "departmentId": 1 }

### [T13] population = 9999999999999 (> Integer.MAX_VALUE) -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": 9999999999999, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T14] population = -5 -> 400 "population: City population must be at least 1 inhabitant."
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": -5, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T15] departmentId = "abc" -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": 5, "departmentId": "abc" }

### [T16] departmentId = 1.9 -> 201 !! truncated to 1 (ACCEPT_FLOAT_AS_INT). Clean up.
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "ZtFloatDept", "population": 5, "departmentId": 1.9 }

### [T17] name = 123 (JSON number) -> 201 !! Jackson coerces to "123". Clean up.
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": 123, "population": 5, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T18] name = {} (object) -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": {}, "population": 5, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T19] id = "abc" in body -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "abc", "name": "Zt", "population": 5, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T20] department code = 34 (number) -> coerced to "34" -> 400 "already exists"
POST {{host}}/departments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": 34, "name": "n" }

### [T21] department code = true -> 201 !! coerced to "true", creates a department. Clean up.
POST {{host}}/departments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": true }

### --- structural junk ---

### [T22] JSON array instead of object -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

[ { "name": "Zt", "population": 5, "departmentId": 1 } ]

### [T23] duplicate keys -> 201, last value wins ("Zb"). Clean up.
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Za", "name": "Zb", "population": 5, "departmentId": 1 }

### [T24] trailing garbage after the JSON -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Zt", "population": 5, "departmentId": 1 }garbage

### [T25] bare string body -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

"hello"

### [T26] bare number body -> 400
POST {{host}}/cities
Content-Type: application/json

42
